## Skills available (13)

Run any with `/<skill-name>`. All are trigger-tuned — the right one usually fires without naming it.

### Planning & design
- `/planning` — concrete implementation plan before any code
- `/spec:create / decompose / execute` — three-stage workflow for big features with code-copy into tasks
- `/ui-planner` — component breakdown, state, flows, a11y, responsive

### Implementation & testing
- `/feature-implementation` — end-to-end feature build; loads references on-demand
- `/write-tests` — unit/integration/e2e with edge-case enumeration
- `/debug` — strict repro → failing test → fix → regression loop

### Quality & review
- `/validate-and-fix` — auto-discover lint/typecheck/test, parallel run, categorize, fix
- `/code-review` — correctness/security/coverage, severity-grouped findings
- `/write-docs` — READMEs, ADRs, runbooks, inline docs, API refs

### Ship & maintain
- `/git:commit` — read repo style, match convention, write specific message
- `/pr` — pre-flight lint/test, structured title/body/test-plan/rollback
- `/checkpoint:create / restore / list` — named git-stash snapshots
- `/dependency-upgrade` — one-at-a-time safe bumps with changelog + suite

## Subagents available

Dispatch them to parallelize work and keep the main session's context clean.

### Always-on
- `test-runner` — iterates failing tests until green (own context, can write code)
- `reviewer` — read-only self-review before PR; structured findings
- `researcher` — gathers external context (docs, PRs, blog posts) without touching code
- `refactoring-expert` — Fowler-style behavior-preserving incremental loop
- `security-auditor` — OWASP-driven deeper-than-review security pass

### Stack-gated (installed only when your stack triggers the gate)
<!-- The installer copies these into `.claude/agents/` only if the stack detects frontend / database / docker. -->
- `accessibility-expert` — WCAG/ARIA/keyboard/a11y tooling (frontend)
- `design-reviewer` — UI/UX post-build review (frontend)
- `database-expert` — query plans, indexes, N+1, migration safety (DB)
- `docker-expert` — multi-stage, caching, size, hardening (Docker)

## Hooks active in this repo

Deterministic guarantees, not prompts. See `.claude/settings.json` for the wiring.

### PreToolUse
- **file-guard** — blocks reads/writes of `.env`, SSH keys, cloud creds — including through shell pipelines like `find | xargs cat`. Override with `FILE_GUARD_OVERRIDE=1`.
- **pre-write-lint** — runs the project linter on files being edited; blocks the tool call on failure.

### PostToolUse
- **check-code-quality** — flags `// ...` placeholder stubs, silent `any`/`as any`, `_foo` unused-param drift that lint won't catch.
- **post-write-test** — runs adjacent tests (`foo.test.ts`, `test_foo.py`, etc.) after each edit.

### Stop
- **create-checkpoint** — git-stash snapshot of the working tree. Restore later with `/checkpoint:restore`.
- **session-summary** — structured log of files changed + commits to `.claude/logs/session-YYYYMMDD.log`.

